AUDIO: 'step in between and nobody owning it afterwards. Most companies can\'t tell you how many of these are running right now. If you run a platform team or you\'re on security or you\'re the person who gets the call when customer data leaks, stay until the end because I\'m'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'going to show you three ways that this breaks then what it looks like when the platform enforces the rules instead of hoping the model remembered. Okay. So, to understand why this keeps happening, you have to understand a term'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that\'s been floating around for a while now. And that\'s called shadow AI. It sounds kind of scary and technical, but it\'s really pretty simple. If you think back about 10 years ago, your company gives you some slow, clunky, unofficial'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'software to do your job. So, what do you do? Well, you just quietly start using Dropbox or Google Sheets or whatever, right? On your own software without asking anyone. Now, IT has no idea and that\'s basically what\'s called shadow'

[01:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'IT. Employees that are using tools that the company never approved and to be honest, they never even knew about. Now, shadow AI is pretty much the exact same thing. Except now, it\'s not Dropbox or Google Drive, it\'s AI, right? And here\'s'

[01:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the part that makes this a much bigger deal. People aren\'t just using an app anymore. They\'re actually building their own apps using AI. In an afternoon, they\'re plugging in real company data and putting that into a production app.'

