VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'both of the options were not great. You could either ban it, which just doesn\'t work because people are going to do it anyways on their own personal accounts, or you could allow it and just accept everything that I just showed you. Or, you know, manually review all of the code yourself.'

[09:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Now, Superblocks is this third option. So, you can build apps by prompting the same way that you would with like Lovable or Replit, but the apps that you deploy actually go inside of your own AWS account with its own database inside of your own VPC. So, it inherits your'

[09:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'network, your identity, your encryption, and all of your audit controls, and your users come in through the SSO that you already use. Now, with Lovable or Replit, your app runs on their infrastructure. Here, it runs on your'

